 "description": "Audit a DNS zone against the rules that make a zone illegal or make it quietly not work. Reports a CNAME at the apex, which is forbidden because the apex must also carry SOA and NS; a CNAME alongside any other record type; an MX, NS or CNAME pointing at a name that is itself a CNAME, whose failure is intermittent rather than total; a target inside the zone the zone does not define; a cyclic CNAME chain; TTLs that differ within one record set; and a record outside the zone. Pay 200000 atomic USDC on Base via exact x402. MCP does not pay; it provides a challenge handoff.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "contract": {
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "example": {
     "forbid_wildcards": true,
     "max_ttl": 86400,
     "min_ttl": 300,
     "required": [
      {
       "name": "example.test",
       "type": "MX"
      },
      {
       "name": "_dmarc.example.test",
       "type": "TXT"
      }
     ]
    },
    "properties": {
     "forbid_wildcards": {
      "description": "Report a wildcard record, which answers for every undefined name. Defaults to false.",
